course: dictionary
lesson: 7572
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. The word preserve can mean keeping something safe, or it can mean jam. «We must preserve old buildings for our grandchildren.» The clue is old buildings, so preserve means keep safe from harm.
explain: Food words are clues too. «She made strawberry preserves for the picnic.» Strawberries and a picnic tell you that preserves means fruit cooked with sugar. Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it, then try that meaning in the sentence.
explain: Preserve can also be a noun, meaning an area kept for wild animals. «The lions live in a game preserve.» Check which job the word does in the sentence: to preserve is a verb (something you do), while a preserve is a noun (a thing).
fact: Preserve (verb) means to keep something safe from harm, damage or change, such as «preserve wildlife».
fact: Preserve (verb) also means to treat food so it lasts a long time, by drying, salting, freezing or pickling.
fact: Preserves (noun) means jam or fruit cooked with sugar to keep, as in «strawberry preserves».
fact: A preserve (noun) is an area kept for wild animals, or something that belongs to only one group.
fact: «Well preserved» means kept in good condition, so a fossil can be well preserved in rock or ice.
exercise: «We must preserve the forest so the birds can live there.» What does preserve mean here? | *To keep safe from harm | To cook with sugar | To cut down for wood | To hunt
exercise: «Mum put the spare fruit in the freezer to preserve it.» What does preserve mean here? | *To keep food from going bad for a long time | To paint it bright colours | To break into small pieces
exercise: «She spread strawberry preserves on her toast.» What are preserves in this sentence? | A park for wild animals | A kind of toast | *Jam made from fruit and sugar | Old buildings
test: «The lions roam freely in the game preserve.» What is a game preserve? | *An area kept for wild animals | A kind of jam | A bridge over a river | Lions' hiding place inside a house
test: «The fossil was well preserved in the rock for millions of years.» What does well preserved mean? | Put in a jar | Badly broken | Hidden under the sea | *Kept in good condition, with little damage
exam: Which sentence uses preserve as a verb meaning keep safe? | *We must preserve the old bridge for everyone | Her preserves won a prize at the show | The game preserve was full of deer | The strawberry preserves were sweet
